  "title": "Headless build in Brett's AmberX-AXF repo (worktree, branch claude/shot-groups).",
  "asked": "Headless build in Brett's AmberX-AXF repo (worktree, branch claude/shot-groups). Read CLAUDE.md + _claude/shared/rules/RULES.md. Opus, one session. Git auth is in your environment (GIT_CONFIG_*); just git push. 0. Wait (poll every 30 s, max 60 min) until origin/main contains the Screenshots tab build (git log origin/main --oneline | grep -i 'shots-tab\\|Screenshots tab', or origin/claude/shots-tab is an ancestor). Then git merge origin/main. Brett: UI Review's Screenshots will fill up fast. When Claude sends shots for him, it must ASK HIM FOR A NAME and file them in a named, timestamped GROUP so he can find them. 1. Groups: {id, name, createdAt (timestamp), source, session/build/agent, app, note}. Every screenshot belongs to exactly one group. Intake API + CLI (framework/cli/shot.mjs) take --group <name> (creates the group if new; same name same day reuses it). No group given -> auto name '<source/session> - <YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm>'. 2. Screenshots tab: group list first (newest first) showing name, timestamp, count, source, cover thumbnail; search by name/date/app/source; tap opens the group's shots. Rename, merge two groups, move shots between groups, delete group. Framework grid + controls, theme/scale tokens only, compact. 3. Rule in _claude/shared/rules/RULES.md: before Claude (any session, voice or chat) sends screenshots for Brett, it asks him for a group name (offer a default like 'Breakroom check - Oct 31 8:20 PM'); headless sessions name the group after their build. 4. Migrate existing shots (e.g. Breakroom check) into a group 'Breakroom check - <their date time>'. Tests (group create/reuse, rename/merge, search, migration). Full local test block from .github/workflows/android.yml + theme/controls/lifecycle checks green. Commit, fetch+merge origin/main, retest, git push origin HEAD:main (retry until it lands). Report at _claude/builds/reports/shot-groups.md.",
